<code>assert !this.contains(\old(this.get(index))) || \old(this.indexOf(\old(this.get(index)))) != index;</code>

However, the above assertion does not fully capture the condition that if the value at the removed index occurred only once, it is absent after removal. A more precise assertion would be:

<code>assert (\old(this.indexOf(\old(this.get(index)))) == \old(this.lastIndexOf(\old(this.get(index))))) && (\old(this.indexOf(\old(this.get(index)))) == index) => !this.contains(\old(this.get(index)));</code>

This ensures that if the value at the removed index was unique (i.e., its first and last occurrence indices are the same and equal to the removed index), then it is no longer present in the vector after removal.
