However, this doesn't fully capture the condition that if the value at the removed index occurred only once, it should be absent after removal. A more accurate representation would be:

<code>assert (\old(this.lastIndexOf(\old(this.get(index)))) == index && \old(this.indexOf(\old(this.get(index)))) == index) => !this.contains(\old(this.get(index)));</code>

This ensures that if the value at the removed index was unique (i.e., its first and last occurrence indices are the same and equal to the removed index), then it should not be present in the vector after removal.
